{"title":"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Each side of the large square in the figure is trisected (divided into three equal parts).  The corners of an inscribed square are at these trisection points, as shown.  The ratio of the area of the inscribed square to the area of the large square is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/9/f69a1c109464f1f5fc9c655bbee9a93db750e4e6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(3,0)--(3,3)--(0,3)--cycle); draw((1,0)--(1,0.2)); draw((2,0)--(2,0.2)); draw((3,1)--(2.8,1)); draw((3,2)--(2.8,2)); draw((1,3)--(1,2.8)); draw((2,3)--(2,2.8)); draw((0,1)--(0.2,1)); draw((0,2)--(0.2,2)); draw((2,0)--(3,2)--(1,3)--(0,1)--cycle); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f137dda89e944971994c3eaff173bb540a25c3e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ \\dfrac{5}{9} \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ \\dfrac{2}{3} \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ \\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{3} \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ \\dfrac{7}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"379\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> unit as the distance from vertex of the large square to the closest trisection point.  Then the large square has side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so its area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  \n</p><p>Each of the four right triangles shown has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc61cbcdf5d4f4f63cb353a9569b6bac52f37352.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 1 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"90\" height=\"37\" />, so the area of the small square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/f/9af82c4b3c4ccdba2413f93d0b11d728dd2b2a1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 - 4\\cdot 1 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"95\" height=\"13\" />.  The ratio of the areas of the two squares is thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47cb52c309c5848672404bb9242effbe4bb6710a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{5}{9}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"60\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the side of the big square be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e634348f8df9eaeac4ced35db64d08a906532e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />.  The area of this square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c38bd9f4c8562a83143f2714cacf228b10ef40a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x\\cdot 3x = 9x^2$\" width=\"102\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>You can use the Pythagorean Theorem on the any of the right triangles to find the length of the side of the inscribed square.  One leg is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, while the other leg is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />.  Thus, the length of the hypotenuse <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, which is also the side of the inscrubed square, is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/b/7fbd4264fbec874b1c14992abd59ea22d4daf604.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + b^2 = c^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/a/83acdfd6d242668444bc29e15f53225210bba4eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + (2x)^2 = c^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/d/c5d10fa7410f323cc35a42676455ffc61af615ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + 4x^2 = c^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/8/b58a7d56bfb0664700e0329e455c58be6eb073c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x^2 = c^2$\" width=\"65\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Once you get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/6/2b693026c70424da68ed4c52d3d0d35d9548ee4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c^2$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" />, you can stop, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/6/2b693026c70424da68ed4c52d3d0d35d9548ee4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c^2$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> is the area of the inscribed square.  The ratio of the areas  of the small square to the big square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/a/97a3c5b41fc5b2988ed61ce9869bfba2a469f1b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5x^2}{9x^2} = \\frac{5}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"66\" height=\"39\" />, giving option <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2e33ab9a00e021af49e888212645d4667903c49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Fill in the gridlines of the diagram.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/7/c77a7100520b1630b2bfbee335f873fedd60d17f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(3,0)--(3,3)--(0,3)--cycle); draw((1,0)--(1,3)); draw((2,0)--(2,3)); draw((3,1)--(0,1)); draw((3,2)--(0,2)); draw((1,3)--(1,0)); draw((2,3)--(2,0)); draw((0,1)--(3,1)); draw((0,2)--(3,2)); draw((2,0)--(3,2)--(1,3)--(0,1)--cycle); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>Let each grid space have length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The inscribed square consists of four congruent triangles and one square.\n</p><p>The triangles each have area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/b/a4b718952713990c68d974715216e494a1040366.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 2\\cdot 1=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"38\" />, and in total they cover <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/f/49f921208b0d70d81ab59f9dab3a50f8ad7351db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\cdot 1 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> square units of area. The central square's area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/b/a4b1047e8bc248cabef7c03e2df7df9e3274379a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\cdot 1=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, the area of the inscribed square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/1/8d1784175ccab2b055588d760e77de61bb46da93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+1=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The big square contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/0/c9047977a9bd03c451567fa47fddf838db16c91d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\cdot 3=9$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> square units of area. Thus, the ratio is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/c/e7cee4c1bc083c3979f7ac19ac9f8646a3d0a29e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2e33ab9a00e021af49e888212645d4667903c49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME\" title=\"1997 AJHSME\">1997 AJHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=1997\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_8_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 8 Problems and Solutions\"> All AJHSME/AMC 8 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AJHSME\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AJHSME\">AJHSME</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AJHSME_Problems_and_Solutions\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AJHSME Problems and Solutions\">AJHSME Problems and Solutions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competition resources\">Mathematics competition resources</a></li></ul>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016193942\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.036 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.054 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 219/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2302/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 132/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5856/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.335      1 -total\n 57.66%    7.113      1 Template:AJHSME_box\n 40.41%    4.985      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:9914:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016193942 and revision id 288127. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}